[00:00:51.908] Server  LOG     Heloooooooooooooooooo Pinecone Response: "{\n  \"result\": {\n    \"hits\": [\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"57\",\n        \"_score\": 0.524254322052002,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Giving feedback to an employee \\n\\n\\nGiving feedback to a superior \\nGiving feedback to a coworker\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"499\",\n        \"_score\": 0.4777154326438904,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Receiving feedback from an employee \\n\\n\\nReceiving feedback from a coworker\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"379\",\n        \"_score\": 0.44260525703430176,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Feedback must be factual, evidence-based, and unbiased.\\n6.3 Review Discussion\\nA one-on-one review discussion must be conducted.\\nThe discussion should cover strengths, improvement areas, and future goals.\\n7. Performance Ratings\\nRatings are assigned based on defined rating scales.\\nRating definitions must be clearly communicated.\\nForced or guided distribution may be applied, if required.\\n8. Feedback Guidelines\\nFeedback should be constructive, specific, and balanced.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"377\",\n        \"_score\": 0.40346142649650574,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Performance reviews may be conducted annually, bi-annually, or quarterly, as defined by the organization.\\nMid-cycle or interim reviews may be conducted to provide ongoing feedback and course correction.\\n4. Review Participants\\nSelf-Review: Employees are required to complete a self-assessment.\\nManager Review: Reporting managers evaluate employee performance.\\nSkip-Level / Panel Review (if applicable): Senior managers or review panels may participate to ensure objectivity.\\n5. Review Criteria\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"343\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3901388347148895,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Communicate the availability of these channels and ensure that employees are aware of the process for submitting queries or concerns.\\nDesignate responsible personnel to address employee queries promptly and professionally.\\nMaintain a log of employee inquiries and resolutions for future reference and process improvement.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"624\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3879452347755432,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Goals are set at the beginning of the performance cycle.\\nGoals must be SMART (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound).\\nGoals are mutually agreed upon by the employee and reporting manager.\\n4.2 Continuous Performance Monitoring\\nManagers are expected to provide ongoing feedback throughout the performance cycle.\\nEmployees are encouraged to seek clarification and support when required.\\nMid-cycle reviews may be conducted to track progress.\\n4.3 Performance Review and Evaluation\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"899\",\n        \"_score\": 0.38647592067718506,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Regular check-ins with manager\\nFeedback and support sessions\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"378\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3804089426994324,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Performance reviews are based on the following criteria:\\nAchievement of KRAs / OKRs\\nQuality of work and productivity\\nBehavioral competencies and values\\nCollaboration and communication\\nInitiative and problem-solving\\n6. Review Process\\n6.1 Self-Assessment\\nEmployees must complete self-reviews within the defined timeline.\\nSelf-assessments should include achievements, challenges, and development needs.\\n6.2 Manager Assessment\\nManagers assess performance against predefined goals and competencies.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"626\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3803965747356415,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"The organization reserves the right to normalize ratings to ensure consistency and fairness.\\n6. Feedback and Development\\nPost-review discussions will be conducted to share feedback and agree on development plans.\\nIndividual Development Plans (IDPs) may be created to address skill gaps and career aspirations.\\nTraining, mentoring, or coaching may be recommended based on performance outcomes.\\n7. Linkage to Rewards and Career Progression\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"1012\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3678995370864868,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Employees may be required to sign a service agreement for high-cost or long-term programs.\\n9. Evaluation of Training Effectiveness\\nTraining effectiveness may be assessed through feedback, assessments, or performance improvement.\\nEmployees may be required to share learning outcomes or apply learnings on the job.\\n10. Roles and Responsibilities\\n10.1 Employees\\nTake ownership of learning and development.\\nActively participate in approved training programs.\\n10.2 Managers\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"345\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3656039834022522,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Use feedback and data analysis to identify strengths, weaknesses, and areas of improvement.\\n12.2 Seek feedback from stakeholders and address any identified areas of improvement:\\nCollect feedback from relevant stakeholders, including employees, HR, Finance, and management, regarding their experience with the payroll process.\\nConduct surveys, interviews, or focus groups to gather feedback and suggestions for improvement.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"380\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3653513193130493,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Both positive achievements and improvement areas must be discussed.\\nFeedback must focus on behavior and outcomes, not personal traits.\\n9. Development Planning\\nIndividual Development Plans (IDPs) may be created post-review.\\nDevelopment actions may include training, mentoring, or stretch assignments.\\nCareer aspirations should be discussed during the review.\\n10. Review Documentation\\nAll reviews must be documented in the performance management system.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"498\",\n        \"_score\": 0.36111563444137573,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Receiving feedback from a superior\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"1026\",\n        \"_score\": 0.35781145095825195,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"5. Performance Evaluation\\nPerformance will be reviewed periodically by the reporting manager.\\nFeedback may be provided through informal check-ins or formal reviews.\\nKey performance expectations may be documented at the start of the probation period.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"625\",\n        \"_score\": 0.35738205909729004,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Formal performance reviews are conducted at the end of the performance cycle.\\nPerformance evaluation is based on goal achievement, competencies, behaviors, and values.\\nSelf-assessment by employees may form part of the review process.\\n5. Performance Rating\\nEmployees will be assigned a performance rating based on predefined criteria.\\nRating scales may include categories such as Outstanding, Exceeds Expectations, Meets Expectations, Needs Improvement, etc.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"207\",\n        \"_score\": 0.35731518268585205,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Step 2: Informal Resolution (Optional but Encouraged)\\nTimeline: As early as possible\\nEmployee may:\\nDiscuss the issue directly with the concerned individual, OR\\nApproach the reporting manager or HR for guidance\\nOutcome:\\nIf resolved → Process closed\\nIf unresolved / inappropriate → Proceed to formal grievance\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"628\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3445112109184265,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"9. Roles and Responsibilities\\n9.1 Employees\\nActively participate in goal setting and performance discussions.\\nTake ownership of assigned goals and development plans.\\n9.2 Reporting Managers\\nSet clear expectations and provide timely feedback.\\nConduct fair and unbiased performance evaluations.\\n9.3 Human Resources\\nFacilitate the performance management process.\\nEnsure consistency, fairness, and compliance with policy.\\n10. Appeals and Review\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"963\",\n        \"_score\": 0.343770831823349,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"4. TIMING AND MODE\\nExit interview to be conducted between resignation acceptance and Last Working Day (LWD)\\nPreferred modes:\\nOne-on-one discussion with HR\\nOnline / written exit feedback form\\nFor senior roles, a leadership-level interaction may be scheduled\\n5. ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"355\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3407628834247589,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Demonstrate commitment toward improvement.\\nAttend review meetings and follow agreed action plans.\\n7.2 Reporting Manager\\nProvide clear expectations and continuous feedback.\\nOffer guidance, support, and resources.\\nDocument progress and discussions.\\n7.3 Human Resources\\nFacilitate the PIP process and ensure fairness.\\nMaintain documentation and compliance.\\n8. Review and Monitoring\\nRegular review meetings will be conducted during the PIP period.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"890\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3390488922595978,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"KRA and OKR performance contributes to overall performance ratings.\\nOutcomes may influence compensation, incentives, promotions, and career development.\\n10. Roles and Responsibilities\\n10.1 Employees\\nOwn and actively track their KRAs and OKRs.\\nCommunicate progress and challenges proactively.\\n10.2 Reporting Managers\\nProvide guidance, feedback, and support.\\nEnsure alignment with team and organizational objectives.\\n10.3 Human Resources\\nDefine and govern the framework.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"86\",\n        \"_score\": 0.33868247270584106,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"6. Informal Resolution\\nEmployees are encouraged, where appropriate and safe, to attempt to resolve concerns informally by:\\nDiscussing the matter directly with the concerned individual, or\\nSeeking guidance from their immediate manager or another member of management\\nIf the concern involves the employee’s reporting manager or if informal discussion is not feasible, the employee may approach Human Resources (HR) or another designated manager.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"765\",\n        \"_score\": 0.33855411410331726,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Ask politely: \\\"How can I assist you today?\\\" or \\\"Who are you here to meet?\\\"\\nIf the visitor has a scheduled appointment, immediately call/notify the employee to announce arrival\\nIf the visitor requires assistance from a colleague, confirm availability before directing them\\nProvide clear directions and, if possible, escort them to their destination\\nFor after-hours or unscheduled visitors, follow the Workplace Visitor Policy\\nMaintain a professional tone and demeanor at all times\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"353\",\n        \"_score\": 0.33832964301109314,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Clearly identify performance gaps\\nProvide focused guidance and support\\nSet measurable improvement expectations\\nOffer a fair opportunity to improve performance\\n4. When a PIP is Initiated\\nAn employee may be placed on a PIP under the following circumstances:\\nConsistent performance ratings of Needs Improvement\\nFailure to meet KRAs / OKRs\\nRepeated feedback indicating performance deficiencies\\nBusiness-critical performance concerns\\n5. PIP Duration\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"629\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3375670909881592,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Employees may raise concerns regarding performance ratings through the defined grievance or appeal process.\\nAll appeals must be submitted within [specified timeframe] after communication of results.\\n11. Confidentiality\\nPerformance data and evaluation outcomes are confidential and will be shared only with authorized stakeholders.\\n12. Policy Compliance\\nNon-compliance with this policy may result in corrective or disciplinary action.\\n13. Policy Review and Amendments\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"346\",\n        \"_score\": 0.33571088314056396,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Analyze the feedback received and identify common themes or areas requiring attention.\\nDevelop action plans to address the identified areas of improvement and implement necessary changes to enhance the payroll process.\\n12.3 Stay updated with changes in legislation and adapt the process accordingly:\\nStay abreast of changes in labor laws, tax regulations, and other statutory requirements that impact payroll processing.\\nRegularly review updates from regulatory authorities and government agencies.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"962\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3353709578514099,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Strengthen retention, culture, and people practices\\nEnsure feedback is collected ethically and confidentially\\n3. EXIT INTERVIEW GUIDELINES\\nExit interviews are conducted for learning and improvement, not for grievance resolution\\nParticipation is encouraged but voluntary\\nFeedback must be captured in a neutral, non-judgmental manner\\nIndividual responses are treated as confidential and used in aggregated form\\nExit interview outcomes do not impact Full & Final settlement or relieving documents\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"382\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3341943323612213,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Provide clear and actionable feedback.\\n12.3 Human Resources\\nGovern and monitor the review process.\\nEnsure consistency and policy compliance.\\n13. Ethical Conduct and Bias Prevention\\nDiscrimination or bias of any kind during reviews is prohibited.\\nReviewers must adhere to organizational values and ethics.\\n14. Non-Compliance\\nFailure to comply with these guidelines may result in corrective action.\\n15. Review and Amendments\\nThe organization reserves the right to revise these guidelines as needed.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"363\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3290589153766632,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Job-specific technical knowledge\\nProblem-solving and analytical skills\\n4.2 BEHAVIORAL AND CULTURAL FIT\\nCommunication and interpersonal skills\\nTeamwork and collaboration\\nIntegrity, ethics, and values alignment\\n4.3 ROLE AND POTENTIAL FIT\\nAbility to meet current role requirements\\nLearning agility and adaptability\\nLeadership or growth potential (where applicable)\\n5. INTERVIEW FEEDBACK AND SCORING\\nInterviewers must record feedback for each stage\\nUse standardized evaluation forms or HRMS tools\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"965\",\n        \"_score\": 0.32891595363616943,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Individual identifiers to be removed in analytics and reporting\\nData usage strictly for organizational improvement\\n8. EXIT INTERVIEW FORM – STANDARD FORMAT\\nEmployee Details\\nEmployee Name (Optional): __________________________\\nEmployee ID: __________________________\\nDepartment / Function: __________________________\\nDesignation: __________________________\\nLast Working Day: __________________________\\nSection A – Overall Experience\\n1. How would you rate your overall experience with the organization?\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"381\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3285715878009796,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Review records are confidential and accessible only to authorized personnel.\\n11. Appeals and Clarifications\\nEmployees may seek clarification or raise concerns regarding review outcomes.\\nAppeals must be submitted within [defined timeframe] of the review discussion.\\n12. Roles and Responsibilities\\n12.1 Employees\\nParticipate actively and honestly in the review process.\\nAccept feedback and work on agreed development actions.\\n12.2 Managers\\nConduct fair, timely, and objective reviews.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"967\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3285471796989441,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"What could the organization have done differently to retain you?\\n__________________________________________________\\nSection D – Reason for Exit\\n7. Primary reason for leaving (select all that apply):\\n Career growth  Compensation  Role mismatch  Work-life balance  Personal reasons  Management  Other: __________\\nSection E – Open Feedback\\n8. Any suggestions or feedback you would like to share?\\n__________________________________________________\\n9. REPORTING AND REVIEW\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"356\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3255172073841095,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Progress will be documented and shared with the employee.\\nAdjustments may be made based on progress, if required.\\n9. Successful Completion of PIP\\nSuccessful completion occurs when performance meets defined expectations.\\nThe employee will be formally notified in writing.\\nContinued performance monitoring may follow.\\n10. Unsuccessful Completion of PIP\\nFailure to meet improvement expectations may lead to further action, including:\\nExtension of PIP\\nRole change or reassignment\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"364\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3239269554615021,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Overall recommendation to be clearly stated:\\nSuitable\\nSuitable with development needs\\nNot suitable\\n6. SELECTION AND APPROVAL\\nFinal selection decision based on consolidated interview feedback\\nHiring manager provides selection justification\\nHR validates process compliance and compensation alignment\\nApproval obtained as per Recruitment Policy approval matrix\\n7. OFFER RELEASE\\nOffers to be issued only by HR\\nCompensation must align with approved budget and grade band\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"295\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3216298818588257,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Employee Opinion Survey Template\\n\\nDear Employee,\\n\\nWe value your feedback and would like to take a few moments of your time to complete this survey. Your answers will be confidential and will help us understand your thoughts and opinions about our company and work environment. Thank you for your participation.\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"71\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3189959228038788,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"[Employee Name] demonstrated professionalism, dedication, and commitment in the discharge of [his/her/their] duties. [He/She/They] maintained good conduct throughout the tenure of employment.\\nWe wish [Employee Name] all the best in [his/her/their] future professional endeavors.\\nFor [Company Name]\\n\\nName: [Authorized Signatory]\\nDesignation: [Title]\\nDate: [Date]\\n\\nCOMPANY VISION, MISSION & VALUES\\n(Corporate Charter & Culture Document)\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"87\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3174174726009369,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"7. Formal Grievance Procedure\\n7.1 Submission of Complaint\\nIf informal resolution is unsuccessful or inappropriate, the employee may submit a formal written complaint to HR or the designated Grievance Redressal Authority.\\nThe complaint should include:\\nDescription of the issue\\nDates and locations of relevant incidents\\nNames of persons involved and witnesses (if any)\\nAny supporting documentation\\nSteps already taken to resolve the matter\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"205\",\n        \"_score\": 0.31633466482162476,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"4. Roles and Responsibilities\\n4.1 Employee\\nRaise concerns promptly and in good faith\\nCooperate during inquiry or investigation\\nMaintain confidentiality\\nRefrain from retaliation\\n4.2 Reporting Manager\\nAttempt informal resolution where appropriate\\nEscalate matters to HR if unresolved or sensitive\\nEnsure no retaliation\\n4.3 Human Resources (HR)\\nAcknowledge and register grievances\\nConduct or coordinate investigations\\nEnsure statutory compliance\\nRecommend corrective or disciplinary actions\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"211\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3161829113960266,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Step 8: Decision & Resolution\\nManagement reviews findings and decides on:\\nMediation or corrective action, OR\\nDisciplinary action (if substantiated)\\nPossible actions include:\\nVerbal or written warning\\nPerformance Improvement Plan (PIP)\\nTraining or counselling\\nTransfer or role change\\nSuspension\\nTermination (as per law)\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"935\",\n        \"_score\": 0.3161330819129944,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Name: [Authorized Signatory]\\nDesignation: [Title]\\nDate: [Date]\\n\\nEmployee Acknowledgement\\nI acknowledge receipt of this warning letter.\\nSignature: _______________________\\nName: ___________________________\\nDate: ___________________________\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"_id\": \"297\",\n        \"_score\": 0.31444182991981506,\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"text\": \"Neither agree nor disagree\\nDisagree\\nStrongly disagree\\n4. How satisfied are you with your immediate co-workers and team?\\nThe answer should be a single choice:\\nVery satisfied\\nSatisfied\\nNeutral\\nDissatisfied\\nVery dissatisfied\\n5. How would you rate the communication between management and employees?\\nThe answer should be a single choice:\\nExcellent\\nGood\\nAverage\\nPoor\\nVery Poor\\n6. Do you feel that management is approachable and willing to listen to your concerns?\\nThe answer should be a single choice:\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"readUnits\": 1,\n    \"embedTotalTokens\": 9\n  }\n}"
